  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Realising rights by mobilising fair extractive sector revenues in Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the program is focused on reducing inequality and improved realization of human rights as a result of more progressive, transparent and accountable mobilization and use of extractive sector revenues in sub -Saharan Africa. The project looks to ensure that extraction -affected communities and community -based organizations in Kenya are able to demand greater accountability from their governments for the mobilization and use of extractive sector taxation revenues; that civil society organizations effectively influence government authorities in Kenya to improve resource mobilization from the extractive sector through a combination of increased transparency, closing legal loopholes that facilitate tax avoidance and more effective enforcement of tax and revenue collection policy and on the regional level, Civil Society Organisations (CSOs) successfully engage with African Union (AU) institutions as well as relevant international forums, to promote further cooperation within Africa to end extractive sector related tax avoidance and illicit financial flows. The project will be implemented in Kwale, Taita Taveta and Kilifi Counties, through partner organizations working in these counties, from 2023 to 2025.</narrative>
  </description>
